3. Platform-Related Security & SPI Shared Responsibility
The Cloud Security Alliance (CSA) Stack Model
Security responsibilities and risks propagate upward through the cloud delivery layers: IaaS → PaaS → SaaS. 
As control shifts from consumer to provider, user management decreases while vendor responsibility increases.
  +-------------------------------------------------------+
  |              Software as a Service (SaaS)            |  <- Consumer controls Data/Access
  +-------------------------------------------------------+  <- Provider controls App & Infra
  |              Platform as a Service (PaaS)            |  <- Consumer controls App Code
  +-------------------------------------------------------+  <- Provider controls OS & Runtime
  |           Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS)         |  <- Consumer controls OS & Apps
  +-------------------------------------------------------+  <- Provider controls Hardware & VMM
	Software as a Service (SaaS) Security: Focuses on data confidentiality in multitenant spaces, application vulnerabilities 
											(OWASP Top 10), identity provisioning/deprovisioning, and compliance with regulations like 
											GDPR and HIPAA6more_horiz.
	Platform as a Service (PaaS) Security: Focuses on secure coding practices, protecting developer SDKs/APIs, 
											middleware security, and Cloud Access Security Broker (CASB) integration925.
	Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS) Security: Focuses on mitigating misconfigured storage buckets (e.g., S3), operating system hardening,
											virtual firewall management, and hypervisor-level isolation926.
